'' T32, RUN: 'new T( a, b )' over a type with no constructor ignored its arguments and
'' returned a calloc-zeroed object -- 'new Point( 3, 4 )' gave 0 0, where fbc fills the
'' fields in order. It now uses the field-by-field initialiser 'base( ... )' uses, inside
'' new's null guard: a short list zeroes the rest, a record-typed field takes a value of
'' its type, and placement new works the same way. Plain data only: a type that needs
'' construction takes no field list (fbc's error 99). Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/new-field-list.bas -o tests/codegen/newfieldlist.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/newfieldlist.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/newfieldlist.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3 4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 7 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1 2 9
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 5 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 8 0
